==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|derely}}, {{m|enm|deorliche}}, from {{inh|en|ang|dēorlīċe|t=worthily, richly}}, equivalent to {{af|en|dear|-ly}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdɪɹli/}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdɪəli/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-dearly.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In a dear or precious manner.
#: {{ux|en|the funeral of our '''dearly''' beloved sister}}
# In a [[dear]] or expensive manner.
#: {{ux|en|a '''dearly''' priced item}}
# At great [[expense]].
#: {{ux|en|He paid '''dearly''' for his mistake.}}

